from pathlib import Path
import json,html,re
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;D=json.loads((R/'course.json').read_text())
content='''<nav><a href="/">← Aleph</a></nav><section class="hero"><p class="eyebrow">Calculus · Thirty study days</p><h1>Understand, practise, then repair.</h1><p class="sub">A three-phase calculus review. Phase 1 is ready below; Phases 2 and 3 are the next stages of the plan.</p><p>Days are relative study days. No calendar start or submission deadline has been assigned.</p></section><div class="phase-grid"><section><h2>1 · Refresher</h2><p>Days 1–10. Exposition, worked examples, five practice problems, a fresh exit check, and a big-picture mind map each day.</p></section><section id="phase2"><h2>2 · Standard problem types</h2><p>Days 11–20. Build a problem-type library across ISI MSQE, IIT JAM, CMI, DSE MA Economics and GATE DA. Match the relevant exam scope and distinguish genuine past questions from original companion problems. Material not yet authored.</p></section><section><h2>3 · Review and remedy</h2><p>Days 21–30. Use Phase 2 submissions to select targeted repairs, worked corrections, fresh transfer checks and delayed reattempts. The exact daily mix will depend on the errors observed. Material not yet authored.</p></section></div><section class="panel"><h2>Start with the meaning, then learn the move</h2><p>Work through an explanation before attempting practice. Follow worked examples with a pencil: name the problem, choose the method, check its conditions, carry out the calculation, and interpret the result. Then close the example and solve a nearby problem independently.</p><p>The limits and integrals lessons contain broader reference banks, not just two examples. IVT has twelve original applications; MVT has twelve companion examples linked to the twelve lessons in your selected playlist. Use a subset in the first sitting and return to the rest. Covering every example and video can take longer than one sitting.</p><p>Upload your work from <strong>Aleph → Subjects → Calculus: 30-day review</strong>. Each study day has its own upload and feedback controls. Scratchpad text on these reading pages stays on the current browser; export it before moving devices. A submission does not establish mastery.</p><p><a class="button" href="day-01.html">Begin Day 1: limits</a></p></section><section class="panel"><h2>Phase 1 · The ten lessons</h2><ol class="toc">'''
for d in D:content+=f'<li><a href="day-{d["day"]:02}.html">Day {d["day"]} · {html.escape(d["title"])}</a><p>{html.escape(d["goal"])}</p></li>'
content+='''</ol><p>Days 9 and 10 deliberately use the repeated topic from the requested list: first the foundations, then applications and consolidation. Monotone convergence here concerns real sequences.</p></section><section class="panel"><h2>The course’s big picture</h2><svg class="mindmap" viewBox="0 0 1000 450" role="img" aria-label="Calculus course concept map"><title>How the ten refresher topics connect</title><rect x="10" y="170" width="210" height="90" rx="12" fill="#176955"/><text x="115" y="220" fill="white" text-anchor="middle" font-size="25">Calculus</text><g stroke="#7896a4" stroke-width="2" fill="none"><path d="M220 215 C300 215 300 55 370 55"/><path d="M220 215 C300 215 300 165 370 165"/><path d="M220 215 C300 215 300 275 370 275"/><path d="M220 215 C300 215 300 385 370 385"/></g><g fill="#edf4f7" stroke="#adc1cb"><rect x="370" y="10" width="615" height="90" rx="8"/><rect x="370" y="120" width="615" height="90" rx="8"/><rect x="370" y="230" width="615" height="90" rx="8"/><rect x="370" y="340" width="615" height="90" rx="8"/></g><g fill="#1f3641" font-family="system-ui" font-size="21"><text x="390" y="43">Limits → continuity → IVT existence</text><text x="390" y="76">Local approach and the values a function must attain</text><text x="390" y="153">Derivatives → MVT → monotonicity and convexity</text><text x="390" y="186">Local slope controls global change and graph shape</text><text x="390" y="263">Integrals → signed accumulation → geometric area</text><text x="390" y="296">Leibniz connects differentiation with accumulation</text><text x="390" y="373">Sequences → series → power series and Taylor</text><text x="390" y="406">Convergence decides when infinite descriptions work</text></g></svg><p>Theorems are bridges between these descriptions. IVT gives existence from continuity; MVT turns slope into total change; FTC connects accumulation and differentiation; sequence theorems control limiting processes.</p></section><section class="panel" id="sources"><h2>Sources and scope</h2><ul><li><a href="https://www.stewartcalculus.com/tec/books/6et/">Stewart Calculus: official chapter and topic index</a> — scope reference for limits and techniques of integration. Edition numbering varies; this course uses topic names.</li><li><a href="https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLlwePzQY_wW9m5oabUf6hvfVfAaA9uAwM">Selected MAT137 MVT playlist</a> — twelve lessons linked in order on Day 5, paired with original companion examples.</li><li><a href="https://mathpop.com/pages/calculus-spivak-4th-edition-table-of-contents">Spivak, Calculus, fourth edition: publisher’s contents</a> — Chapter 11 appendix, Convexity and Concavity, pp. 219–229. Day 6 is an original geometric reading companion, with a dictionary for strict versus weak convexity.</li><li><a href="https://admission.isical.ac.in/Syllabus/MSQE-Syllabus-2026.pdf">ISI MSQE 2026 syllabus</a> — includes calculus and convexity among its mathematical topics.</li><li><a href="https://jam2026.iitb.ac.in/files/syllabus_MA.pdf">IIT JAM Mathematics 2026 syllabus</a> — the broad sequence, series and real-analysis reference for this refresher.</li><li><a href="https://www.cmi.ac.in/admissions/syllabus/datascience-syllabus.pdf">CMI MSc Data Science syllabus</a> — elementary calculus is within the stated scope; this is the programme assumed from the existing prep context.</li><li><a href="https://gate2026.iitg.ac.in/doc/GATE2026_Syllabus/DA_2026_Syllabus.pdf">GATE DA 2026 syllabus</a> — its calculus/optimization scope is narrower than the union of topics here.</li><li><a href="https://www.du.ac.in/uploads/new-web/24122025-AC-1025-Appendix-28.pdf">University of Delhi programme and CUET paper mapping</a> and <a href="https://exams.nta.nic.in/cuet-pg/syllabus/common/">NTA CUET-PG common-subject syllabi</a> — distinguish current MA Economics preparation from historical DSE entrance-paper practice in Phase 2.</li></ul><p>All exercises and worked companion examples in these notes are original; they are not presented as copied textbook exercises or verified past examination questions. Mathematical exposition uses common calculus results with their conditions made explicit.</p></section>'''
# Match the authored standalone page shell.
page=runpy=None
(R/'index.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Calculus: thirty-day review · Aleph</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="/psets/material-page.css"><link rel="stylesheet" href="style.css"></head><body><main class="wrap">'+content+'</main></body></html>')
